(g) recover  the  arrear  taxes    by  attaching  and  selling,  in  the  prescribed  
manner,  any  of  the  defaulting  taxpayer’s  immovable  property    and  
by seizing and selling any of his movable property; or  
(h) take  a  take  a  security  deposit  from  a  guarantor  of  the  defaulting 
taxpayer in such manner and on such terms as may be prescribed. 
(6) In  relation  to  the  recovery  of  arrear  taxes  by  a  Customs  Commissioner,  
